  "notes": [
    "No board edited. Analytic screen only, not native DRC or impedance validation.",
    "Preserve original bridge copper and its UUIDs rather than recreate duplicates. Bridge entries here are present solely for mutual screening.",
    "Replace all upstream and downstream USB routing that conflicts with the new full topology; parent owns completion beyond the listed output handoff.",
    "A/B USB-C joins are the only unavoidable branches; no protection bypass, bridge-center launch, or dead-ended stubs is included.",
    "Donor retains .127mm signal width; no power widths or ground contacts change.",
    "Ordinary through vias have .45mm diameter/.20mm drill; all new via drills clear pasted SMD pads.",
    "Alternative replaces lower J6 excursion, adds one net USB through via versus baseline, uses short In1 DP and In3 DM joins; these launches are not continuously coupled.",
    "All VBUS_C connections preserved: complete replacement of one via plus its three incident paths. CC1 is unaffected.",
    "VBUS_C via foreign-pad minimum gap is near 0.130mm, so preserve exact coordinates and verify manufacturing/native DRC margins."
